This PR makes it possible to nest statements to easier build sophisticated custom models.

All statements have a new `do` operation that allows a list of statements. See the documentation custom-models.md on how to use this.

(The original suggestion was with a `then` keyword, but this was a bit inconsistent for the `else` keyword - click details:)

<details>

The `if` and `else_if` statements have a `do` entry that allows a list of statements:

```json
{ 
  "if": "country == DEU",
  "do": [
     { "if": "road_class == PRIMARY", "multiply_by": "0.8"  }
  ]
}
```

And `else` allows this list directly:

```json
{ "if": "max_speed > 70", "limit_to": "70" },
{ "else": "", 
  "do": [
     { "if": "road_class == PRIMARY", "multiply_by": "0.8"  }
  ]
}
```

Further nesting is currently possible (maybe we should limit it to 2 levels?):

```json
{ 
  "if": "country == DEU",
  "do": [
     { 
         "if": "road_class == PRIMARY",
         "do": [
            { "if": "max_speed > 70", "multiply_by": "0.5" }
         ]
     }
  ]
}
```

</details>

